      "verify": "Interleaved A/B/A/B in one binary, medians; check the delta holds at both the grid-starved and the oversubscribed batch; re-profile and confirm MFMA-tiles-per-wave and per-stage kernel time moved - mean occupancy per CU can FALL while that stage gets 10% faster, so occupancy is the wrong confirmation.",
      "caution": "It is an interior optimum, not a monotone trend - halving once won, halving again fell back to ~1.05x overall, and the same halving on the sibling stage (24 K-iterations, nothing to amortise) cost 13.4%; also verify each stage's K-iteration count before carrying the change across stages, and gate on SNR before timing, since tile / MFMA-shape variants in block-scaled families can compile, run, and still return numeric garbage.",
